<td id="S4.T4.fig1.6.5.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><span id="S4.T4.fig1.6.5.4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">7.55 <math id="S4.T4.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pm" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>±</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pm</annotation></semantics></math> 5.74</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S4.T4.fig1.6.6" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S4.T4.fig1.6.6.1" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_bb"><span id="S4.T4.fig1.6.6.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">SSD-Mamba2 (Ours)</span></th>
<td id="S4.T4.fig1.6.6.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb"><span id="S4.T4.fig1.6.6.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">537.67 <math id="S4.T4.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pm" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>±</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pm</annotation></semantics></math> 307.79</span></td>
<td id="S4.T4.fig1.6.6.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb"><span id="S4.T4.fig1.6.6.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">193.70 <math id="S4.T4.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pm" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>±</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pm</annotation></semantics></math> 93.61</span></td>
<td id="S4.T4.fig1.6.6.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb"><span id="S4.T4.fig1.6.6.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">10.50 <math id="S4.T4.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pm" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>±</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pm</annotation></semantics></math> 5.36</span></td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</figure>
<div id="S4.SS5.SSS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS5.SSS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">From Fig. <a href="#S4.F4" title="Fig. 4 ‣ IV-E1 Performance vs. Baselines ‣ IV-E Experiment Results ‣ IV Experiments ‣ Can SSD-Mamba2 Unlock Reinforcement Learning for End-to-End Motion Control?" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>, <em id="S4.SS5.SSS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">SSD-Mamba2</em> shows a steeper early slope, higher asymptotic return, and tighter confidence band than all baselines.
Numerically (Table <a href="#S4.T4.fig1" title="TABLE IV ‣ IV-E1 Performance vs. Baselines ‣ IV-E Experiment Results ‣ IV Experiments ‣ Can SSD-Mamba2 Unlock Reinforcement Learning for End-to-End Motion Control?" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">IV</span></a>), <em id="S4.SS5.SSS1.p2.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">SSD-Mamba2</em> improves return over <em id="S4.SS5.SSS1.p2.1.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Transformer Proprio-Vision</em> from <math id="S4.SS5.SSS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="354.4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>354.4</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">354.4</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S4.SS5.SSS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="537.7" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>537.7</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">537.7</annotation></semantics></math> (+<span id="S4.SS5.SSS1.p2.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">51.7</span>%), reduces collisions from <math id="S4.SS5.SSS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="202.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>202.5</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">202.5</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S4.SS5.SSS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="193.7" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>193.7</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">193.7</annotation></semantics></math> (–<span id="S4.SS5.SSS1.p2.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">4.3</span>%), and increases distance from <math id="S4.SS5.SSS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="7.55" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>7.55</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">7.55</annotation></semantics></math> m to <math id="S4.SS5.SSS1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10.50" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>10.50</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10.50</annotation></semantics></math> m (+<span id="S4.SS5.SSS1.p2.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">39.1</span>%).
These results indicate both higher peak performance and more stable optimization.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS5.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection"><span id="S4.SS5.SSS2.6" class="ltx_text">IV-E</span>2 </span><span id="S4.SS5.SSS2.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Ablation: Effect of Multi-Modality</span></h4>

<div id="S4.SS5.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS5.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Single-modality agents perform poorly.
<em id="S4.SS5.SSS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Proprio-Only</em> achieves a return of <math id="S4.SS5.SSS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="56.3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>56.3</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">56.3</annotation></semantics></math>, with <math id="S4.SS5.SSS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="571.2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>571.2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">571.2</annotation></semantics></math> collisions and only <math id="S4.SS5.SSS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3.29" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>3.29</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3.29</annotation></semantics></math> m traveled.
Vision-only agents barely progress: <em id="S4.SS5.SSS2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Transformer Vision-Only</em> reaches a return of <math id="S4.SS5.SSS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="13.4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>13.4</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">13.4</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S4.SS5.SSS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1.27" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1.27</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1.27</annotation></semantics></math> m distance, while <em id="S4.SS5.SSS2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Mamba2 Vision-Only</em> yields <math id="S4.SS5.SSS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="16.8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>16.8</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">16.8</annotation></semantics></math> return and <math id="S4.SS5.SSS2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1.54" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1.54</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1.54</annotation></semantics></math> m distance.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS5.SSS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS5.SSS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Adding vision to proprioception provides substantial gains.
<em id="S4.SS5.SSS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Transformer Proprio-Vision</em> improves over <em id="S4.SS5.SSS2.p2.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Proprio-Only</em> by raising return from <math id="S4.SS5.SSS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="56.3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>56.3</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">56.3</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S4.SS5.SSS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="354.4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>354.4</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">354.4</annotation></semantics></math> (+<span id="S4.SS5.SSS2.p2.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">529</span>%), reducing collisions from <math id="S4.SS5.SSS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="571.2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>571.2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">571.2</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S4.SS5.SSS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="202.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>202.5</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">202.5</annotation></semantics></math> (–<span id="S4.SS5.SSS2.p2.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">64.5</span>%), and increasing distance from <math id="S4.SS5.SSS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3.29" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>3.29</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3.29</annotation></semantics></math> m to <math id="S4.SS5.SSS2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="7.55" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>7.55</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">7.55</annotation></semantics></math> m (+<span id="S4.SS5.SSS2.p2.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">129.5</span>%).
It also outperforms <em id="S4.SS5.SSS2.p2.1.6" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Transformer Vision-Only</em>, achieving a return more than <span id="S4.SS5.SSS2.p2.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">25.4</span> <math id="S4.SS5.SSS2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>×</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\times</annotation></semantics></math> higher (<math id="S4.SS5.SSS2.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="354.4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>354.4</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">354.4</annotation></semantics></math> vs. <math id="S4.SS5.SSS2.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="13.4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>13.4</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">13.4</annotation></semantics></math>) and a distance nearly <span id="S4.SS5.SSS2.p2.1.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">6</span> <math id="S4.SS5.SSS2.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>×</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\times</annotation></semantics></math> longer (<math id="S4.SS5.SSS2.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="7.55" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>7.55</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">7.55</annotation></semantics></math> m vs. <math id="S4.SS5.SSS2.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1.27" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1.27</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1.27</annotation></semantics></math> m), while providing meaningful collision reduction.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS5.SSS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS5.SSS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Our proposed <em id="S4.SS5.SSS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">SSD-Mamba2</em> further amplifies these benefits.
Compared with <em id="S4.SS5.SSS2.p3.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Mamba2 Vision-Only</em>, it delivers over <span id="S4.SS5.SSS2.p3.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">30</span> <math id="S4.SS5.SSS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>×</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\times</annotation></semantics></math> higher return (<math id="S4.SS5.SSS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="537.7" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>537.7</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">537.7</annotation></semantics></math> vs. <math id="S4.SS5.SSS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="16.8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>16.8</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">16.8</annotation></semantics></math>) and about <span id="S4.SS5.SSS2.p3.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">6.8</span> <math id="S4.SS5.SSS2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>×</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\times</annotation></semantics></math> longer distance (<math id="S4.SS5.SSS2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10.50" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>10.50</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10.50</annotation></semantics></math> m vs. <math id="S4.SS5.SSS2.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1.54" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1.54</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1.54</annotation></semantics></math> m).
Relative to <em id="S4.SS5.SSS2.p3.1.5" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Proprio-Only</em>, it boosts return nearly <span id="S4.SS5.SSS2.p3.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">9.5</span> <math id="S4.SS5.SSS2.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>×</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\times</annotation></semantics></math> (<math id="S4.SS5.SSS2.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="537.7" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>537.7</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">537.7</annotation></semantics></math> vs. <math id="S4.SS5.SSS2.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="56.3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>56.3</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">56.3</annotation></semantics></math>) while cutting collisions by <span id="S4.SS5.SSS2.p3.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">66%</span> (<math id="S4.SS5.SSS2.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="193.7" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>193.7</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">193.7</annotation></semantics></math> vs. <math id="S4.SS5.SSS2.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="571.2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>571.2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">571.2</annotation></semantics></math>).</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS5.SSS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS5.SSS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">These results confirm that multi-modality is essential for foresightful locomotion.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS5.SSS3" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection"><span id="S4.SS5.SSS3.6" class="ltx_text">IV-E</span>3 </span><span id="S4.SS5.SSS3.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Ablation: Effect of the Fusion Backbone</span></h4>

<div id="S4.SS5.SSS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS5.SSS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Among vision-only agents, <em id="S4.SS5.SSS3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Mamba2 Vision-Only</em> provides modest gains over <em id="S4.SS5.SSS3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Transformer Vision-Only</em>, improving return from <math id="S4.SS5.SSS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="13.4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>13.4</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">13.4</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S4.SS5.SSS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="16.8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>16.8</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">16.8</annotation></semantics></math> (+<span id="S4.SS5.SSS3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">25.4</span>%) and distance from <math id="S4.SS5.SSS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1.27" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1.27</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1.27</annotation></semantics></math> m to <math id="S4.SS5.SSS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1.54" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1.54</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1.54</annotation></semantics></math> m (+<span id="S4.SS5.SSS3.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">21.3</span>%). However, both remain far from the performance of multi-modal agents.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS5.SSS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS5.SSS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">For multi-modal inputs, <em id="S4.SS5.SSS3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">SSD-Mamba2</em> outperforms <em id="S4.SS5.SSS3.p2.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Transformer Proprio-Vision</em>, increasing return from <math id="S4.SS5.SSS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="354.4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>354.4</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">354.4</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S4.SS5.SSS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="537.7" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>537.7</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">537.7</annotation></semantics></math> (+<span id="S4.SS5.SSS3.p2.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">51.7</span>%), raising distance from <math id="S4.SS5.SSS3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="7.55" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>7.55</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">7.55</annotation></semantics></math> m to <math id="S4.SS5.SSS3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10.50" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>10.50</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10.50</annotation></semantics></math> m (+<span id="S4.SS5.SSS3.p2.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">39.1</span>%), and slightly lowering collisions from <math id="S4.SS5.SSS3.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="202.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>202.5</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">202.5</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S4.SS5.SSS3.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="193.7" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>193.7</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">193.7</annotation></semantics></math> (–<span id="S4.SS5.SSS3.p2.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">4.3</span>%).</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS5.SSS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS5.SSS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Overall, the backbone choice becomes decisive once multi-modal inputs are available: SSD-Mamba2 delivers more effective fusion and superior control outcomes than attention-based fusion under the same training protocol.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS5.SSS4" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection"><span id="S4.SS5.SSS4.6" class="ltx_text">IV-E</span>4 </span><span id="S4.SS5.SSS4.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Generalization to Unseen Conditions</span></h4>

<div id="S4.SS5.SSS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS5.SSS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A central challenge for quadrupedal controllers is whether policies trained in one environment can transfer to unseen conditions without fine-tuning.
We therefore train all agents in <em id="S4.SS5.SSS4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Thin Obstacle &amp; Goals</em> and evaluate them zero-shot in two novel scenarios: <em id="S4.SS5.SSS4.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Rugged Terrain with Thin Obstacles &amp; Goals</em> and <em id="S4.SS5.SSS4.p1.1.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Sphere Obstacles &amp; Goals</em>.
These settings introduce irregular surfaces and altered obstacle geometry, testing the robustness and foresight of the learned policies.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S4.T5.fig1" class="ltx_table ltx_minipage ltx_align_center ltx_align_middle" style="width:317.4pt;">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="S4.T5.fig1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">TABLE V</span>: </span><span id="S4.T5.fig1.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Zero-shot performance on <em id="S4.T5.fig1.5.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Rugged Terrain with Thin Obstacles &amp; Goals</em>. Mean <math id="S4.T5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pm" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>±</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pm</annotation></semantics></math> std over 10 runs.</span></figcaption>
<table id="S4.T5.fig1.6" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="S4.T5.fig1.6.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S4.T5.fig1.6.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_th_row ltx_border_tt"><span id="S4.T5.fig1.6.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Method</span></th>
<th id="S4.T5.fig1.6.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt"><span id="S4.T5.fig1.6.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Return</span></th>
<th id="S4.T5.fig1.6.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt"><span id="S4.T5.fig1.6.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Collision Times</span></th>
<th id="S4.T5.fig1.6.1.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt"><span id="S4.T5.fig1.6.1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Distance Moved (m)</span></th></tr>
</thead>
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="S4.T5.fig1.6.2" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S4.T5.fig1.6.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_t"><span id="S4.T5.fig1.6.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Proprio-Only</span></th>
